<article class="env-definition" id="02MU">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02MU">Definition <span data-tag="02MU">12.11.1</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{A}$ be an abelian category. We denote $K_0(\mathcal{A})$ the <em>zeroth $K$-group of $\mathcal{A}$</em>. It is the abelian group constructed as follows. Take the free abelian group on the objects of $\mathcal{A}$ and for every short exact sequence $0 \to A \to B \to C \to 0$ impose the relation $[B] - [A] - [C] = 0$. </p>
</article>